# TestOps Manual-to-Autotest Flow

Mandatory process for each new autotest (required):

- Always work in branch `main`.
- Always create a git commit with test changes.
- Always run the new test locally and confirm it passes.
- If any of these three steps is skipped, the task is not considered done.

When user asks to create a new autotest from a manual TestOps testcase:

- First fetch testcase list with `expand: ["status"]` and identify current status taxonomy used in project.
- Do not rely on workflow names because workflow taxonomy can differ across projects.
- Use `automated = false` as the only required baseline filter for manual-to-autotest candidate selection.
- Determine automation-ready statuses dynamically from current project statuses.
- Consider status names as automation-ready when they clearly indicate preparation for automation, for example:
  - `To Automate`, `For Automation`, `Automation Candidate`, `Ready for Automation`
  - Russian equivalents like `На автоматизацию`, `К автоматизации`, `Для автоматизации`, `Готов к автоматизации`
- If several status variants match, show all matching statuses and ask user which one to use for this run.
- If no status name clearly maps to automation intent, always show available statuses and ask user to choose automation-ready status explicitly.
- Build candidate list only from testcases that match selected automation-ready status + `automated = false`.
- Ask user which testcase to start with.
- Multiple testcases can be implemented sequentially in `main` when requested.
- For selected testcase, request `expand: ["code"]` to get step structure.
- Implement Playwright test code based on testcase steps.
- Keep metadata aligned with TestOps: `@allure.id` in test title, feature/story labels.
- Run new test locally and confirm it passes (mandatory).

Before commit:

- Check current git branch.
- Create flow must run on branch `main`.
- If current branch is not `main`, stop and ask user to switch to `main` first.

Delivery steps:

- Create a git commit with new test changes (mandatory).
- Push current branch to remote (`git push -u origin HEAD` on first push) before TestOps run.
- Run testcase in TestOps on current branch.
- Pass branch via `jobsParams` with fixed parameter name `Branch`.
- Wait for completion and report final status.
